## 3. Walkthrough & Exam Drills

### Drill 1: Deploy Storage Provisioner (`01-provisioners/`)

1. **Deploy Local Path Provisioner**:

   ```bash
   {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/01-provisioners/install-local-path-provisioner.sh
   kubectl get pods -n local-path-storage
   ```

### Drill 2: Apply StorageClasses & Dynamic PVC (`02-storage-classes/`)

1. **Deploy StorageClasses**:

   ```bash
   kubectl apply -f {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes/cka-lab-sc-retain.yaml
   kubectl apply -f {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes/cka-lab-sc-delete-wait.yaml
   kubectl get storageclass
   ```

1. **Create Dynamic PVC & Inspect Delayed Binding**:

   ```bash
   kubectl apply -f {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes/cka-lab-dynamic-pvc.yaml
   kubectl get pvc cka-lab-dynamic-pvc
   ```

1. **Create Consumer Pod & Verify Bound Phase**:

   ```bash
   kubectl apply -f {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes/cka-lab-consumer-pod.yaml
   kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready pod/cka-lab-storage-consumer --timeout=60s
   kubectl get pvc,pv
   ```

1. **Verify Volume Expansion**:

   ```bash
   kubectl patch pvc cka-lab-dynamic-pvc -p '{"spec":{"resources":{"requests":{"storage":"200Mi"}}}}'
   kubectl get pvc cka-lab-dynamic-pvc
   ```

### Drill 3: Dynamic NFS CSI Driver & Shared ReadWriteMany Storage

1. **Deploy Kubernetes NFS CSI Driver**:

   ```bash
   {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/01-provisioners/install-nfs-csi-driver.sh
   kubectl get csidrivers
   ```

1. **Apply Dynamic NFS StorageClass**:

   ```bash
   kubectl apply -f {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes/03-nfs-csi-sc.yaml
   kubectl get storageclass {{ cka_lab_nfs_csi_storage_class | default('nfs-csi') }}
   ```

1. **Create Dynamic ReadWriteMany PVC & Verify Immediate Binding**:

   ```bash
   kubectl apply -f {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes/04-nfs-dynamic-pvc.yaml
   kubectl get pvc nfs-dynamic-claim
   ```

1. **Deploy Multi-Replica Workload & Verify Shared Data**:

   ```bash
   kubectl apply -f {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes/05-nfs-shared-deployment.yaml
   kubectl rollout status deployment/nfs-shared-app --timeout=60s
   kubectl get pods -l app=nfs-shared-app -o wide
   ```

1. **Test Online PVC Expansion (500Mi -> 1Gi)**:

   ```bash
   kubectl patch pvc nfs-dynamic-claim -p '{"spec":{"resources":{"requests":{"storage":"1Gi"}}}}'
   kubectl get pvc nfs-dynamic-claim
   ```

### Drill 4: Cloud-Native Ceph Dynamic Shared Storage Alternatives

When using Ceph as the cluster storage backend (`storage_nfs_provider: "ceph"`), candidates and administrators have two cloud-native alternatives for dynamic ReadWriteMany shared storage:

#### Approach A: Ceph NFS via NFS CSI (`03-ceph-nfs-sc.yaml`)

Consumes the Ceph NFS-Ganesha daemon export (`nfs-server.local:/exports`) using the standard NFS CSI driver:

1. **Apply Ceph NFS StorageClass**:

   ```bash
   kubectl apply -f {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes/03-ceph-nfs-sc.yaml
   kubectl get storageclass {{ cka_lab_ceph_nfs_storage_class | default('ceph-nfs-csi') }}
   ```

1. **Deploy Dynamic RWX PVC & Multi-Replica Workload**:

   ```bash
   kubectl apply -f {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes/04-ceph-dynamic-pvc.yaml
   kubectl apply -f {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes/05-ceph-shared-deployment.yaml
   kubectl rollout status deployment/ceph-nfs-shared-app --timeout=60s
   ```

#### Approach B: Native CephFS Shared Filesystem (`03-cephfs-sc.yaml`)

Directly uses Ceph's native distributed filesystem driver (`rook-ceph.cephfs.csi.ceph.com`), bypassing NFS translation layers:

1. **Apply Native CephFS StorageClass**:

   ```bash
   kubectl apply -f {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes/03-cephfs-sc.yaml
   kubectl get storageclass {{ cka_lab_cephfs_storage_class | default('rook-cephfs') }}
   ```

